			<item>
				<title>React Native Debug</title>
				<link>https://example.org/2025/react-native-debug/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 05 Dec 2025 03:17:31 +0600</pubDate>
				<guid>https://example.org/2025/react-native-debug/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;So I had to execute some native code inside a React Native application that uses Expo, but none of the methods seemed to work properly. Because the packages and libraries hadn’t been updated, they didn’t work well with the current Expo SDK version. I don’t know much about mobile application development, but while debugging and searching for solutions, I realized there’s a lot I can learn about it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Eventually, we settled on using gomobile, which builds an XCFramework for iOS and an AAR file for Android, along with the corresponding bindings. Then we’ll patch some packages and use JSON-RPC to achieve what we were trying to do. I spent two days debugging the issue and learned quite a lot in the process.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
